{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\nouicompat\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}}\viewkind4\uc1\pard\sa120\f0\fs22 {\b\fs32 Prescriptive Specification -- Plan-Set Sale Edition}\par CMA Residence -- Birmingham, Alabama -- 2026 -- Issue 1.0\par\par {\i These notes accompany a set of construction drawings prepared by CMA and conveyed to the purchaser for use on a single residence. CMA provides design documents only; CMA does not administer or observe the construction. The purchaser, owner, and the licensed builder of record are wholly responsible for execution, code compliance, means and methods, and the safety and adequacy of the work. These notes establish the minimum standards CMA requires of any home built from its drawings.}\par\par {\b\fs26 01  General Conditions & Scope of Drawings}\par {\b Documents conveyed.}  The drawings, schedules, and these notes together constitute CMA's design documents. They convey design intent and prescribe minimum finish, material, and assembly standards. They are not a contract between CMA and any builder. CMA is not a party to the construction contract.\par {\b No construction administration.}  CMA will not perform site visits, submittal review, RFI response, change-order review, punch lists, or any other construction-administration service unless engaged separately under a written supplemental agreement. Absent such an agreement, no advice, comment, or silence by CMA shall be construed as approval of any work.\par \par {\b\fs26 02  Drawing Interpretation & Precedence}\par {\b Order of precedence.}  Where conflict exists among the documents, the more stringent requirement applies. Among themselves, the documents are read in this order: written addenda or revisions; large-scale details; small-scale details and elevations; plans; schedules; these notes. Written dimensions govern over scaled measurements. Do not scale drawings.\par \par {\b\fs26 03  Site Documentation & Existing Conditions}\par {\b Field verification.}  All existing conditions, dimensions, elevations, setbacks, easements, and utility locations shall be verified by the builder before excavation, fabrication, or ordering. The drawings rely on information furnished to CMA at the time of issue and are not a survey.\par \par {\b\fs26 04  Contractor Qualifications & Licensing}\par {\b Builder of record.}  The work shall be performed by a builder properly licensed by the State of Alabama Home Builders Licensure Board (Alabama Code \u167?34-14A) and registered in the project's jurisdiction. The builder shall carry general liability and builder's-risk insurance and shall name the owner as an additional insured.\par \par {\b\fs26 05  Submittals & Approval Timelines}\par {\b No CMA review.}  Under this edition, CMA does not receive, review, stamp, or approve submittals, shop drawings, samples, or product data. The builder and owner shall jointly review and approve all such items before fabrication or order.\par \par {\b\fs26 06  Material Standards & Substitutions}\par {\b Standard quality.}  All materials shall be new, unused, of first quality, and free of defects. No reclaimed, salvaged, or seconds material unless expressly indicated on the drawings.\par {\b CMA standing requirements.}  Half-round copper gutters and round copper downspouts. Copper flashing at all roof transitions, valleys, drip edges, pitch breaks, chimneys, beam caps, and roof-to-wall conditions. Copper or lead-coated copper pans at all through-wall and shower conditions. Stainless steel or silicon-bronze fasteners at all exterior wood, brick mold, porches, decks, rafter tails, and any concealed fastening in contact with treated lumber. No exposed galvanized fasteners on visible exterior surfaces.\par {\b Substitutions.}  Items shown on the drawings or named in these notes are required. Any substitution is the owner's and builder's decision and shall be documented in writing between them. CMA does not warrant the equivalence of any substituted product, and substitution does not transfer any design liability to CMA.\par \par {\b\fs26 07  Workmanship Standards}\par {\b Standard of work.}  All work shall be performed by tradesmen skilled and experienced in the work of their trade, in a manner consistent with the highest standard of residential custom construction. Lines true, surfaces plumb and level, joints tight and consistent, reveals uniform.\par \par {\b\fs26 08  Change Order Protocol}\par {\b Owner authorization required.}  No change to the design -- including, without limitation, changes to plan, elevation, roof form, opening sizes, exterior material, exterior color, principal interior finish, or structural assembly -- shall be made without written authorization from the owner.\par {\b Field modification risk.}  Field modifications that depart from the drawings are at the builder's and owner's sole risk. CMA's design liability does not extend to work as modified in the field without CMA's written consultation.\par \par {\b\fs26 09  Quality Assurance & Final Inspection}\par {\b Owner-led inspections.}  The owner is encouraged to conduct, directly or through a qualified third-party inspector, a pre-pour foundation review, a pre-drywall framing/MEP/flashing review, and a substantial-completion punch walk before final payment. CMA may be retained for these reviews under separate agreement.\par \par {\b\fs26 10  Code Compliance -- Alabama Residential}\par {\b Applicable codes.}  All work shall comply with all codes, standards, and regulations in force in the project's jurisdiction at the time of permit, including without limitation the IRC, IECC, NEC, IPC, and IMC as adopted by the State of Alabama and the local authority having jurisdiction, and any local zoning, historic, or overlay-district requirements.\par \par }